{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# S3 (a8ea): Config-driven type mapping + type-granular skip\n\n## Context / Problem\nEpic 3d7a adds a config-driven mapping seam (S1: `mapping_config.MappingLayer`, axes\n`status_map/type_map/link_map/priority_map`, `SKIP=\"skip\"`, `resolve_for_project`,\n`validate`). S2 made STATUS config-driven — the template: `config.effective_status_map`\n(`config.py:77`) threads a per-project `status_map` param through the Backend port\n(`_backend.py:372`) into `outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields` (`:108`);\n`rebar-status:` stamp in `outbound_labels.py`; reverse-map-free inbound\n`recover_status_label` (`inbound_fields.py:152`). TYPE is still hard-coded:\n`LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA` (`adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py:40` = `{bug,story,task,epic}`),\n`EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES` (`config.py:13`), with three create sites defaulting an unknown type\nto Jira `Task`/capitalized passthrough. Distinct local types can collapse to one Jira type\n(lossy). Syncable = `get_args(TicketType)` (`types.py:23`) − `EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES` =\n`{bug,epic,story,task}` = keys of `LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA`.\n\n## Approach\nThree outcomes for a local `ticket_type`: **remap** (effective type map), **skip**\n(per-project type-granular exclusion), **FAIL-CLOSED** on an undecided syncable type.\nRound-trip safety: NEW `rebar-type:` annotation label symmetric with `rebar-status:`,\nrecovered reverse-map-free inbound.\n\n### Finding 1 (G7) — fail-closed is LOAD-TIME, not application-time\nThe parent AC (\"load-time fail-closed on undecided types\") is the PRIMARY deliverable.\nWire it at config RESOLUTION, mirroring the offline fail-closed in\n`mapping_config.validate` (its `_check_vocab`/`_check_capability` raise\n`MappingConfigError`):\n- NEW `config.effective_type_map(project_key, root)` mirrors `effective_status_map`\n  (`config.py:77`): `builtin=MappingLayer(type_map=LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA)` ←\n  `resolve_for_project`, drop `SKIP` values.\n- NEW completeness gate `config.effective_type_decision` (or a check inside\n  `effective_type_map`): after resolving, every syncable type\n  (`get_args(TicketType) − EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES`, minus the per-project effective excluded\n  set) must be DECIDED — explicit target OR `SKIP`; else raise `MappingConfigError` AT\n  RESOLUTION (load) time, before any mutation. Application-time raising at the create\n  mappers is a SECONDARY guard only.\n\n### Finding 3 (G6) — reverse TYPE map source for the lossy-stamp rule\n`_desired_type_annotation` stamps only when the forward target does NOT reverse to this\nlocal type — needs a Jira→local TYPE reverse map. `config.py` has none, and\n`outbound_labels.py` imports ONLY `config`. FIX: add NEW `config.jira_to_local_type`\nmirroring `config.jira_to_local_status` (`config.py:64`) — canonical reverse of\n`LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA`, kept in lock-step with `inbound_fields._JIRA_TO_LOCAL_TYPE`\n(`inbound_fields.py:105`) via a parity test. `outbound_labels` imports it from `config`.\n\n### Finding 4 (G6) — thread the effective type map through the Backend port\nMirror S2's `status_map` threading:\n- Add `type_map: dict[str, str] | None = None` to `OutboundMapper.map_local_to_remote`\n  (`_backend.py:372`, beside `status_map`).\n- Add `type_map` to `outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields` (`:101`, beside\n  `status_map` at `:108`); resolve issuetype through it (replacing the\n  `_LOCAL_TO_JIRA_TYPE.get(..., \"Task\")` coerce at `:143`) with fail-closed.\n- Same for `jira_datacenter/backend.py` (coerce at `:86`).\n- NEW `outbound_differ._effective_type_map_for` mirrors `_effective_status_map_for`\n  (`outbound_differ.py:272`); `_compute_outbound_create_mutation`\n  (`outbound_mutation_builders.py:37`) passes `type_map=` into `map_local_to_remote`.\n\n### Finding 2 (G1G2/G6) — acli.py:282 needs a MATERIALLY DIFFERENT rewrite\n`adapters/jira/acli.py:282` (`JiraClient.create_issue`, the transport's OWN method, NOT\nthe `OutboundMapper` port) computes `issue_type = ticket_data.get(\"ticket_type\",\"Task\")\n.capitalize()` — passthrough capitalize, NO map lookup, NO `LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA` import; an\nunknown syncable type (\"spike\") is capitalized and passed through, never coerced to Task.\nFIX (distinct from the two mapper paths): import `LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA`, resolve `issue_type`\nthrough the effective per-project type map (carried on the create payload, e.g. a reserved\nkey beside `_bridge_target_project`), fail-closed on an undecided type.\n\n## Surface-parity census — rebar-type: stamp + inbound recovery + prefix filters\n- Outbound stamp: NEW `outbound_labels._REBAR_TYPE_LABEL_PREFIX=\"rebar-type:\"`,\n  `_desired_type_annotation` (mirror `_desired_status_annotation` `outbound_labels.py:89`,\n  using `config.jira_to_local_type`), `_diff_type_annotation_labels` (mirror `:114`).\n  Threaded at BOTH sites in `outbound_mutation_builders.py`:\n  `_compute_outbound_create_mutation` compute `:81`/merge `:138`;\n  `_compute_outbound_update_mutation` compute `:276`/merge `:281`.\n- Inbound recovery: NEW `inbound_fields.recover_type_label` (mirror `recover_status_label`\n  `:152`) + `_LOCAL_TYPE_VOCAB` DERIVED from `get_args(TicketType)`; applied at\n  `inbound_fields.py:311-313`, label-over-raw like `:326`.\n- Per-project excluded set replaces the single `EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES` read\n  (`outbound_differ.py:377`) at BOTH consumers: `:430` (per-ticket loop) and `:519`\n  (`_compute_outbound_select_absent_gets`).\n- `rebar-type:` added to ALL FOUR prefix tuples: `outbound_labels.py:34`\n  `_EXCLUDED_PREFIXES` (re-export `outbound_differ.py:77`; consumed\n  `outbound_mutation_builders.py:136`); `inbound_collection_diffs.py:88` `_EXCLUDED_PREFIXES`\n  (re-export `inbound_differ.py:31`; read `reconcile_check.py:96`); `differ.py:105`\n  `_BRIDGE_INTERNAL_LABEL_PREFIXES`; `inbound_translate.py:58`\n  `_BRIDGE_INTERNAL_TAG_PREFIXES` (keeps its intentional omission of `\"imported:\"`).\n\n## Scope\n`config.py` (effective_type_map, effective_type_decision, effective_excluded_sync_types,\njira_to_local_type); `mapping_config.py` (NEW syncable-completeness check); `_backend.py`\nport; the 3 create paths (`outbound_fields.py`, `jira_datacenter/backend.py`, `acli.py`);\n`outbound_labels.py`, `outbound_mutation_builders.py`, `outbound_differ.py`,\n`inbound_fields.py`, `inbound_collection_diffs.py`, `differ.py`, `inbound_translate.py`.\nRespect module-size (cap 800 LOC; target 200-500) — additions small.\n\n## Testing\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_type_mapping.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `test_load_time_fail_closed_on_undecided_syncable_type` — resolving an effective type\n  map that leaves a syncable type undecided raises `MappingConfigError` at LOAD time.\n- [ ] `test_skip_is_a_valid_type_decision` — a syncable type mapped to `SKIP` passes the\n  load-time completeness gate and excludes the ticket.\n- [ ] `test_effective_type_map_default_equals_builtin` — no `[mapping]` block ⇒ map equals\n  `LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA`.\n- [ ] `test_effective_type_map_per_project_override` — project `type_map` remaps.\n- [ ] `test_type_skip_excludes_ticket_both_consumers` — excluded at `outbound_differ.py:430`\n  AND `:519`.\n- [ ] `test_type_map_threaded_through_backend_port` — `map_local_to_remote` type_map param\n  reaches `outbound_fields`/`jira_datacenter` and drives issuetype.\n- [ ] `test_acli_create_issue_maps_and_fails_closed` — acli resolves via the type map and\n  raises on an undecided syncable type (no capitalize passthrough).\n- [ ] `test_rebar_type_label_stamped_when_lossy` — collapsing types stamp `rebar-type:` at\n  create and update sites via `config.jira_to_local_type`.\n- [ ] `test_rebar_type_label_recovered_reverse_map_free` — `recover_type_label` restores the\n  original local type from the label.\n- [ ] `test_rebar_type_prefix_excluded_all_four_tuples` — filtered by all four tuples.\n- [ ] `test_jira_to_local_type_parity` — `config.jira_to_local_type` equals\n  `inbound_fields._JIRA_TO_LOCAL_TYPE`.\n- [ ] `test_local_type_vocab_derived_from_ticket_type` — `_LOCAL_TYPE_VOCAB` equals\n  `get_args(TicketType)`.\n\nTest tier: unit"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787355034409649001,"uuid":"a4c4ee0d-3f70-435b-95c0-8ce825c473d6"}